I don't think that is necessary most of the time. There is a huge
difference between characters designed for ranged combat, and
characters designed for melee combat.  Melee characters are designed to
take melee damage.  Granted, my melee characters in the early game will
throw projectiles at monsters like mumaks, there is very little risk
involved with a melee character running straight at most of the
monsters in the game.

It is also important to note that defense sometimes requires killing
things as quickly as possible, which can't be done if you are wasting
time doing small ranged damage.  There are many cases where you can
avoid being mobbed if you run up to the monsters as they are
approaching you, as opposed to wasting time trying to dance around all
of them while throwing projectiles.  This is very important in the
Gnomish Mines, where narrow hallways are sometimes not an option.
Granted, you could just fall back on Elebereth whenever you are about
to get mobbed, this makes the fight take a really long time.  You
probably don't have enough projectiles to kill the whole mob, so you
need to waste turns retrieving the projectiles, while avoiding the mob,
so that you can continue hitting the mob.



